      {
        "id": "source-collinear-addition-and-result",
        "description": "Lower source construction has a immediately followed by b on one horizontal baseline, both pointing right. Separate lower resultant is start/end aligned, points right, and is labelled vector a + vector b.",
        "objects": ["chain-a", "chain-b", "result", "chain-a-text", "chain-b-text", "result-text"],
        "assertions": ["chain-a-connects", "chain-b-connects", "result-connects", "chain-collinear", "result-copy-equal", "result-copy-parallel"]
      },
      {
        "id": "source-internal-point-relationships",
        "description": "All nine defining endpoints and all arrow relations belong wholly to this group. The offset resultant row has the same displacement as the chain. Exact modern regularization gives rightward 180 + 300 = 480 without presenting any numerical ratio as source data.",
